      "body": "## Overview\n\nPreserve six-query speculative grouping when launching Flash's AITER MXFP4 candidate-gather indexer on gfx950. Flattening every query to its own request loses AITER's grouped launch tuning.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Select grouped launches for 32 heads, 16K candidate tokens, and at least 128 rows with six query rows per request.\n- Preserve per-query candidate slots and causal row ends, including padded rows; other shapes retain their existing dispatch.\n- Earlier isolated pipeline measurements at 128K context/request, top-512, 2048 candidate blocks of eight tokens showed 90.33 → 79.68 µs at 192 rows and 174.22 → 144.49 µs at 384 rows. These were HIP graph measurements with reused buffers; they are not cold-HBM or serving throughput claims.\n\n## Validation\n\nMI355X, editable vLLM base `5d35ce3934`:\n\n```bash\nHIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=6 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=6 HF_HOME=/data \\\nFLYDSL_RUNTIME_CACHE_DIR=/data/dsv41-c128-comparison/flydsl_cache \\\n  .venv/bin/python -m pytest \\\n  tests/kernels/attention/test_rocm_paged_mxfp4_indexer.py -q\n```\n\nThe full suite passed: **35 passed**. The added test runs the real indexer pipeline against the Torch reference with variable context lengths, per-query candidates, compression ratios, page sizes 64/128, and a padded request. The MI355X MLA CI mirror runs the suite. Ruff and pre-commit pass.\n\n**Pending:** combined DPATP2 c128 AgentX serving benchmark and model evaluation with native ASM and #57478. No serving throughput gain is claimed before that run completes.\n\n## Details\n\nReuse `decode_native` request metadata and `_Layer.rows` for grouped query views. The gather kernel still receives per-query candidate slots and causal bounds, so grouping changes its launch shape without merging queries' visible tokens.\n\nDuplicate-work check: #57517 introduces AITER paged MXFP4 indexing, while #63888 changes decode top-k initialization. This draft changes only the candidate-gather query grouping in the existing indexer; neither PR implements this dispatch. Searches for grouped indexer and MXFP4 gather found no equivalent open change. Closed #63634 supplied the performance investigation context, but this is Flash-specific grouping rather than its blanket top-k dispatch.\n\n---\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\nAI assistance: Codex implemented and tested this draft at the human author's request. Human line-by-line review and independent validation are pending; this is not ready to merge.\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>**\n",
